      "type": "list_item",
      "source": "When U+200C ZERO WIDTH NON-JOINER is inserted between two characters, it directs the rendering engine to render them separately/disconnected when it might otherwise render them as a ligature. For example, a rendering engine might display “fl” in English as a connected glyph; inserting the zero width non-joiner would force them to be rendered as disconnected glyphs.",
